FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
    Fault : BOOL;
    Ack : BOOL;
    Reset : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    Alarm : BOOL;
    Acknowledged : BOOL;
    Horn : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    previous_fault : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

Do output vars initial false implicitly. Maybe to satisfy initial can explicitly `Alarm : BOOL := FALSE;`? CODESYS allows initializers in VAR_OUTPUT. Could include. Requirement initial. Better explicit. But formal compile support? likely. Typical. Need preserve exact names/case.

Implementation:
IF Reset AND NOT Fault THEN
    Alarm := FALSE;
    Acknowledged := FALSE;
ELSIF Fault THEN
    Alarm := TRUE;
    IF NOT previous_fault THEN
        Acknowledged := FALSE;
    ELSIF Ack THEN
        Acknowledged := TRUE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    IF Alarm AND Ack THEN
        Acknowledged := TRUE;
    END_IF;
END_IF;

Horn := Alarm AND NOT Acknowledged;
previous_fault := Fault;

Does Else branch retain Alarm implicitly yes. Acknowledged likewise except Ack true sets true. In Reset branch Acknowledged false, Alarm false, horn false. Good.

Potential requirement #4 says else retain Alarm, and if Alarm and Ack set ack. If alarm false and acknowledged somehow true? In valid state Acknowledged can't be true if alarm false except maybe previous state after reset both false. Fine. P7 idle no alarm history: If qAlarm false, Fault false, and Reset maybe doesn't matter: P7 says no Fault and no qAlarm -> outputs false even if Ack pressed. Our output if Alarm false initially and qAlarm false, else branch Alarm false, ack not set, Acknowledged stays false. Good.

But potential issue previous_fault updated every scan. yes.

